{
	title: 'Model picker',
	spec: 'Ctrl-M and /model open a modal of models from configured providers, filtered as you type, with sensible ranking (typing opus-5.5 puts claude-opus-5-5 first, not step-3.5-flash). Enter switches the session model (a protocol command, recorded in history); the list comes from the host. Escape closes it; on the web so do a tap outside it and its close button (touch screens have no Escape). The list is a tree (task zg, tasks/w4/forms.md, Model picker); the thinking level in it is a later task.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Opening (forms.md, Provenance): Ctrl-M sends the `models` command and the host answers that client alone with `models { sessionId, current, items }`; `/model` alone replies { say, open: 'models' } and the host broadcasts the same event to every follower. Clients open the picker on any `models` event for the session on screen. `/model <id>` checks models.valid (a registered provider or a synthetic hal/ model, no whitespace; unlisted ids of a known provider are allowed) and calls ctx.setModel, which records a change note (task 29); it reports 'Model changed: <old> → <new>' (efforts included), like /rename and /cd, or 'model: <id> (unchanged)'.",
		'List: host/models.ts asks each provider that has the optional Provider.models(signal) (at most models.timeoutMs, 3 s; successful lists cached models.ttlMs, 1 h; failures not cached) and puts current, default and hal/* first. openai-compat lists GET <base>/models with its key (an endpoint whose key env var is unset is not listed). anthropic lists GET /v1/models with the account headers (anthropic.headers), falling back to anthropic.knownModels() on any failure: whether OAuth tokens may list models was not verified live.',
		'Ranking: common/picker.ts splits query and id into words (letters and digits apart, so opus-5.5 = opus 5 5); every query word must occur in order, scoring word starts, whole words and adjacency; ties go to shorter ids, then host order. Checked against the live OpenRouter list (~300 ids).',
		'Terminal: app.open(modal, submit, onKey?) got an onKey hook (picker.refilter after every key) and submit now receives the modal state. Web: a native <dialog> in page.ts; the search input edits natively (view.search), Enter/Escape/Up/Down go through view.modalKey (modals.step), the dialog cancel event is Escape.',
		'Keep picker coverage focused on user interactions and nontrivial ranking rules. Remove the standalone Opus 5.5 ranking example: the model-search interaction test exercises the same query and verifies the selected command against the same competing model fixture. Remove the empty-query passthrough test, which restates the rank function early return. Retain multiword and whole-word ranking, tree interaction, no-match safety, effort controls and account-catalog/cache regressions.'
